  "name": "Question 9",
  "problem": "Let $L=MN.$ What is the value of ${l}_{22}$, if\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ 4 & 2\\end{aligned}],\\,N=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 3\\end{aligned}]?\n$$\n\n${l}_{22}=$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "Multiplying the $2$nd row in $M$ by the $2$nd column in $N$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{l}_{22} & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ 4 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =4\\cdot 2+2\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =8+6 \\\\  & =14.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
